  kicker="The condition"
  description="Infantile spasms are a severe epilepsy of infancy. Repository corticotropin, a long-acting ACTH gel, is labelled as monotherapy for them in children under two — the strongest of the old Acthar indications, backed by randomised trials rather than case series. Here the peptide is doing its endocrine job: driving cortisol. A 2012 guideline preferred ACTH to vigabatrin in the short term; that guideline is now retired."
