>
  <KeyTakeaways
    items={[
      'Infantile spasms are brief, clustered seizures of infancy, usually with a chaotic EEG pattern called hypsarrhythmia. Developmental injury is common.',
      'Repository corticotropin (Acthar Gel) is FDA-labelled as monotherapy for this condition in children under two. That is a different claim from its older inflammatory labels.',
